## 3. Top findings
- **Your pains overlap with other founders'.** Your trace-digging and wasted-thread cost fall into the "can't see what each run and agent did" cluster (run-opacity), which now has 3 founders, tied for the largest. Your "couldn't tell if it was done" sits next to the "no quality scoreboard" cluster (2 founders).
- **Three of your pains are new clusters, 1 founder each so far:** calls to the wrong agent, context rot within a run, and completion nobody can verify.
- **The top 3 fixes across all 11 founders:**
  1. Trace and cost for each agent thread.
  2. Webhooks when a run fails, plus a timeout for sub-agents that stall.
  3. A stored pass/fail verdict for each agent.
- **Your Linear tickets:** the export has no status field, so I can't tell which bugs or features are still open.

**The one fix that would help you most:** a stored pass/fail verdict for each agent's thread. It would record whether that agent's criteria were met, why, and what the thread cost. That record is the second half of your Monday list. It would have caught the misrouted placeholder straight away (that step fails, and you see what it cost), so you'd no longer need to dig through traces. You can do a rough version now: this run kept a manifest listing each specialist's expected files and a record of every agent thread, and a per-agent check compared them against what actually exists. That's the dashboard's did-its-job table, and it passed 4 of 4. Only the cost column is empty until there's real cost data.

